<aside class="wiki-toc"><div class="wiki-toc-inner"><button aria-expanded="false" class="wiki-toc-toggle" data-wiki-toc-toggle="" type="button"><span data-copy-en="On this page" data-copy-zh="本页目录">On this page</span><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><p class="wiki-toc-heading" data-copy-en="On this page" data-copy-zh="本页目录">On this page</p><div class="wiki-toc-links" data-lang-panel="en" data-wiki-toc-links=""><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-stats">Attributes and skills have different jobs</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-effective-stats">Base attributes, effective values and growth</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-resources">Health, Energy, Calm and Satiation</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-proficiencies">Starting proficiencies and long-term builds</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-careers">Careers, skills and Working Experience</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-learning">Choose a learning route</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-choices">Find a skill for the task</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-combat">Combat</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-magic">Magic</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-social">Social</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-technology">Technology</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-economic">Economic</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-performance">Performance</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-intimate">Intimate</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-culinary">Culinary</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-catalogue-physical">Physical</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-specific-sources">Specific sources and important conditions</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-lesson-reference">Named lesson costs</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-troubleshooting">When a lesson is missing</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#en-related">Related guides</a></div><div class="wiki-toc-links" data-lang-panel="zh" data-wiki-toc-links="" hidden="" lang="zh-CN"><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-stats">先分清属性与技能</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-effective-stats">基础属性、有效属性与成长上限</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-resources">生命、精力、镇定与饱腹感</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-proficiencies">起始专长与长期培养</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-careers">职业、技能与工作经验</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-learning">先选获取方式</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-choices">常用功能从哪里找</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-combat">战斗</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-magic">魔法</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-social">社交</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-technology">科技</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-economic">经济</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-performance">表演</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-intimate">亲密</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-culinary">烹饪</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-catalogue-physical">体能</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-specific-sources">专属来源与特别条件</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-lesson-reference">指定课程费用表</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-troubleshooting">找不到课程或不能学习</a><a class="wiki-toc-h2" href="#zh-related">相关指南</a></div></div></aside>
<article class="wiki-article"><p class="starter-reading-note" data-copy-en="Select a screenshot to enlarge it. Screens show example inventories and progress." data-copy-zh="点击截图可放大查看。图中的库存和进度仅为示例，请以自己的实际情况为准。">Select a screenshot to enlarge it. Screens show example inventories and progress.</p><div class="wiki-source-content wiki-source-content-en" data-lang-panel="en" lang="en"><div class="starter-lead"><p>Skills are normally learned once and retained. Attributes, learned skills, specialist paths and minigame upgrades serve different purposes. This index groups all 132 current catalogue skills as the character sheet does and shows how to obtain them.</p><ol><li>Open the character sheet and select a learned skill for details.</li><li>Choose a named lesson, character route or ordinary random learning.</li><li>Prepare the chosen entry’s own requirements and costs; book thresholds apply to that book selection.</li></ol></div>
<section id="en-stats"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Reliable_general_advice"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Separate_resources_and_progress_trackers"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Skill-unlocked_stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Vocational_stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_ten_primary_stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Player_stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_short_version"></span><h2>Attributes and skills have different jobs</h2><p>Attributes grow through activities, work and rewards; skills are learned abilities. Your starting proficiency sets initial numbers, two skills, equipment, a bedroom action and career access. You can develop other directions afterward.</p><details><summary>Show the 14 ordinary attributes</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Attribute</th><th scope="col">Main uses</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Strength</th><td data-label="Main uses">Physical attacks, strength checks and maximum Health.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Intelligence</th><td data-label="Main uses">Research, technical/economic learning, maximum Calm and starting wealth.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Charm</th><td data-label="Main uses">Social and relationship checks, performance, maximum Calm.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Stamina</th><td data-label="Main uses">Maximum Health, Energy and Satiation; long activities.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ability</th><td data-label="Main uses">Quick attacks, Stormslash, coordination and dexterity checks.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Creativity</th><td data-label="Main uses">Music, performance, creative work and related learning.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Perception</th><td data-label="Main uses">Observation, encounters and perception-based learning.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mystic</th><td data-label="Main uses">Magic damage/healing, rituals and magical learning.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Technology</th><td data-label="Main uses">Technical work, hacking and engineering checks.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Luck</th><td data-label="Main uses">Chance-based activities, games and starting wealth.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cooking</th><td data-label="Main uses">Cooking activities, Chef work and culinary requirements.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Commerce</th><td data-label="Main uses">Business, Broker work, investments and commercial checks.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Communication</th><td data-label="Main uses">Customer-facing work, social routes and Tamer’s requirement.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Rogue</th><td data-label="Main uses">Theft, infiltration, heists and related checks.</td></tr></tbody></table></details><p>Tamer adds Taming at 1; Leadership adds Leadership at 1. Beast, Vampire, Attractiveness, experience, faction Clout and resources each track different progress.</p><figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: The Character sheet separates attributes, current resources, experience and learned skills. Starting values here are an example build." href="../assets/images/wiki/skills-guide/en-wealth-character.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="The Character sheet separates attributes, current resources, experience and learned skills. Starting values here are an example build." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/skills-guide/en-wealth-character.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>The Character sheet separates attributes, current resources, experience and learned skills. Starting values here are an example build.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-effective-stats"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id=".E2.80.9CPermanent_modifier.E2.80.9D_does_not_mean_.E2.80.9Cbase_stat.E2.80.9D"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="“Permanent_modifier”_does_not_mean_“base_stat”"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Temporary_or_state-dependent"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Permanent_ownership.2C_conditional_effect"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Permanent_ownership,_conditional_effect"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Permanent_progression"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Permanent_versus_conditional_modifiers"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Twenty-four-hour_consumable_buffs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Live_percentage_key-item_bonuses"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Is_50_the_stat_cap.3F"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Is_50_the_stat_cap?"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_still_uses_base_values.3F"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_still_uses_base_values?"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_uses_effective_values.3F"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_uses_effective_values?"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Effective-stat_formula"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Base_stats.2C_effective_stats.2C_and_caps"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Base_stats,_effective_stats,_and_caps"></span><h2>Base attributes, effective values and growth</h2><p>An ordinary effective attribute equals its base value plus permanent flat bonuses, active consumable bonuses and owned key-item bonuses. Attractiveness also separates base value from bonuses. Beast can include its temporary bonus; Vampire uses its own base value.</p><p>Some actions appear according to effective values while their final learning or unlock check still uses base values. If a lesson appears but cannot be confirmed, inspect the base attribute. Ordinary attributes have no universal hard cap of 50; activities, jobs and rewards can impose their own growth limits.</p><details><summary>Show key-item percentage attribute bonuses</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Bonus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Magic Spectacles</th><td data-label="Bonus">Intelligence +10%；Attractiveness +10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Awesome Crown</th><td data-label="Bonus">Strength +2%；Intelligence +2%；Charm +2%；Stamina +2%；Ability +2%；Creativity +2%；Perception +2%；Mystic +2%；Technology +2%；Luck +2%；Cooking +2%；Commerce +2%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ornate Locket</th><td data-label="Bonus">Charm +10%；Attractiveness +10%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Each item calculates its percentage from the base value separately, rounds down with a minimum bonus of 1 for each affected attribute, then adds its result. It does not compound another item’s or potion’s bonus.</p></details><details><summary>Show 24-hour temporary attribute bonuses</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Consumable</th><th scope="col">Attribute bonus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Focus</th><td data-label="Attribute bonus">Intelligence, Mystic, Technology and Perception +25 each</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cologne</th><td data-label="Attribute bonus">Charm and Attractiveness +10 each</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Luck</th><td data-label="Attribute bonus">Luck +50; designated activities have additional rolls</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Desire</th><td data-label="Attribute bonus">Beast +50 while Beast Mode applies; also grants 200 Erotic Experience when used</td></tr></tbody></table><p>An already-active effect cannot be consumed again to stack it. These effective-value bonuses do not become permanent base attributes. Other consumables use their own combat or timing effects.</p></details></section>
<section id="en-resources"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Loss-reduction_skills"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Bonuses_applied_after_the_curve"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Progressive_reduction_and_soft_caps"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Raw_resource_formulas"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_shared_raw-stat_total"></span><h2>Health, Energy, Calm and Satiation</h2><p>Health mainly follows Strength and Stamina, Energy depends heavily on Stamina, and Calm mainly follows Charm and Intelligence. Satiation also follows Stamina. Temporary attribute bonuses and ordinary key-item attribute bonuses do not replace base attributes in these formulas.</p><details><summary>Show maximum-resource calculation reference</summary><p>Let S be the sum of ten base attributes: Strength, Intelligence, Charm, Stamina, Ability, Creativity, Perception, Mystic, Technology and Cooking. Luck, Commerce, Communication and Rogue are excluded. Floor brackets mean rounding down.</p><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Resource</th><th scope="col">Value t before the curve</th><th scope="col">Late-curve threshold t</th><th scope="col">Curve approaches</th><th scope="col">Curve rate k</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Health</th><td data-label="Value t before the curve">3 × (Strength + Stamina) + ⌊S/2⌋</td><td data-label="Late-curve threshold t">1,100</td><td data-label="Curve approaches">750</td><td data-label="Curve rate k">0.0025</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Energy</th><td data-label="Value t before the curve">8 × Stamina + ⌊S/2⌋</td><td data-label="Late-curve threshold t">1,300</td><td data-label="Curve approaches">775</td><td data-label="Curve rate k">0.0020</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Calm</th><td data-label="Value t before the curve">3 × (Charm + Intelligence) + ⌊S/2⌋</td><td data-label="Late-curve threshold t">1,100</td><td data-label="Curve approaches">750</td><td data-label="Curve rate k">0.0025</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Through the threshold: P(t)=t−floor[t×(0.10+t/7500+t²/7500000)]. Above threshold a, round P(a)+[approach value−P(a)]×[1−exp(−k×(t−a))] to an integer.</p><p>For Satiation, t=4×Stamina+floor(S/4). Use t through 100; above 100, use 100+floor((t−100)/2). Starting wealth=2×(Intelligence+Luck)+Technology.</p><p>Permanent maximum-resource rewards are added after the curve. An owned Queenstone adds 1 maximum Health per level; Aether Stone adds 1 maximum Energy and Calm per level. Heart of the Ocean and Eye of Batman each add 50 maximum Health, Energy and Calm; Vital Heartcap adds 50 maximum Health. The Second Pulse then multiplies maximum Health by 1.10, followed by Bio-Reactor Core at+1% per level. Mnemonic Battery multiplies maximum Energy at+1% per level. Thus 750/775 are curve approach values, rather than final hard caps after bonuses.</p></details><p>Endurance Training, Inner Peace and Iron Constitution respectively multiply applicable negative Energy, Calm and Health adjustments by 0.90 before that adjustment’s rounding. Combat and special activities can use their own drain handling.</p></section>
<section id="en-proficiencies"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Flexible_completionist_route"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Economy_route"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Magic_route"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Physical_route"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Build_planning"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="How_the_paths_combine_with_exclusive_skills"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Assassin_chain_mechanics"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Rank_thresholds_and_titles"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Earning_specialist_points"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Damage_and_healing_multiplier"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Unlock_requirements"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Specialist_combat_paths"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Patreon_Master"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Jack_of_All_Trades"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Starting_package_and_private_action"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Starting_vocational_stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Starting_primary_stats"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Starting_proficiencies"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Health.2C_energy.2C_calm.2C_satiation.2C_and_starting_wealth"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Health,_energy,_calm,_satiation,_and_starting_wealth"></span><h2>Starting proficiencies and long-term builds</h2><p>Ordinary character creation offers 11 proficiencies and 20 additional points for the ten primary attributes. The tables show base values before those 20 points. Cooking, Commerce, Communication and Rogue use the proficiency’s fixed starting values. Main/secondary/weakness labels describe the starting direction without adding a separate growth-rate bonus to every action.</p><details><summary>Show starting skills, base values and bedroom actions</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Starting proficiency</th><th scope="col">Two starting skills</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Body Builder</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Power Strike / Endurance Training</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Scholar</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Arcane Knowledge / Researching</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Salesman</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Silver Tongue / Networking</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Computer Expert</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Engineering Genius / System Hacking</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Musician</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Musical Virtuosity / Master Performer</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Martial Artist</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Martial Arts / Combat Reflexes</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Player</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Seduction / Reading People</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Games Master</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Tactical Awareness / Cheating</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Athlete</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Endurance Training / Adrenaline Rush</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Magician</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Elemental Blast / Illusion Weaving</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jack of All Trades</th><td data-label="Two starting skills">Improvisation / Cultural Adaptation</td></tr></tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Proficiency</th><th scope="col">Strength</th><th scope="col">Intelligence</th><th scope="col">Charm</th><th scope="col">Stamina</th><th scope="col">Ability</th><th scope="col">Creativity</th><th scope="col">Perception</th><th scope="col">Mystic</th><th scope="col">Technology</th><th scope="col">Luck</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Body Builder</th><td data-label="Strength">29</td><td data-label="Intelligence">8</td><td data-label="Charm">9</td><td data-label="Stamina">21</td><td data-label="Ability">11</td><td data-label="Creativity">12</td><td data-label="Perception">10</td><td data-label="Mystic">1</td><td data-label="Technology">8</td><td data-label="Luck">6</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Scholar</th><td data-label="Strength">7</td><td data-label="Intelligence">30</td><td data-label="Charm">8</td><td data-label="Stamina">10</td><td data-label="Ability">6</td><td data-label="Creativity">18</td><td data-label="Perception">20</td><td data-label="Mystic">12</td><td data-label="Technology">9</td><td data-label="Luck">13</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Salesman</th><td data-label="Strength">8</td><td data-label="Intelligence">11</td><td data-label="Charm">28</td><td data-label="Stamina">10</td><td data-label="Ability">1</td><td data-label="Creativity">9</td><td data-label="Perception">13</td><td data-label="Mystic">6</td><td data-label="Technology">7</td><td data-label="Luck">20</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Computer Expert</th><td data-label="Strength">6</td><td data-label="Intelligence">17</td><td data-label="Charm">8</td><td data-label="Stamina">1</td><td data-label="Ability">15</td><td data-label="Creativity">12</td><td data-label="Perception">9</td><td data-label="Mystic">10</td><td data-label="Technology">27</td><td data-label="Luck">11</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Musician</th><td data-label="Strength">9</td><td data-label="Intelligence">10</td><td data-label="Charm">18</td><td data-label="Stamina">8</td><td data-label="Ability">13</td><td data-label="Creativity">27</td><td data-label="Perception">1</td><td data-label="Mystic">11</td><td data-label="Technology">6</td><td data-label="Luck">12</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Martial Artist</th><td data-label="Strength">15</td><td data-label="Intelligence">8</td><td data-label="Charm">6</td><td data-label="Stamina">15</td><td data-label="Ability">29</td><td data-label="Creativity">2</td><td data-label="Perception">15</td><td data-label="Mystic">13</td><td data-label="Technology">10</td><td data-label="Luck">9</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Player</th><td data-label="Strength">11</td><td data-label="Intelligence">13</td><td data-label="Charm">30</td><td data-label="Stamina">10</td><td data-label="Ability">12</td><td data-label="Creativity">8</td><td data-label="Perception">16</td><td data-label="Mystic">1</td><td data-label="Technology">6</td><td data-label="Luck">18</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Games Master</th><td data-label="Strength">8</td><td data-label="Intelligence">18</td><td data-label="Charm">1</td><td data-label="Stamina">12</td><td data-label="Ability">10</td><td data-label="Creativity">15</td><td data-label="Perception">26</td><td data-label="Mystic">9</td><td data-label="Technology">13</td><td data-label="Luck">29</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Athlete</th><td data-label="Strength">24</td><td data-label="Intelligence">9</td><td data-label="Charm">11</td><td data-label="Stamina">28</td><td data-label="Ability">15</td><td data-label="Creativity">6</td><td data-label="Perception">8</td><td data-label="Mystic">10</td><td data-label="Technology">1</td><td data-label="Luck">12</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Magician</th><td data-label="Strength">7</td><td data-label="Intelligence">15</td><td data-label="Charm">13</td><td data-label="Stamina">9</td><td data-label="Ability">11</td><td data-label="Creativity">22</td><td data-label="Perception">20</td><td data-label="Mystic">28</td><td data-label="Technology">12</td><td data-label="Luck">8</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jack of All Trades</th><td data-label="Strength">12</td><td data-label="Intelligence">16</td><td data-label="Charm">17</td><td data-label="Stamina">13</td><td data-label="Ability">10</td><td data-label="Creativity">18</td><td data-label="Perception">11</td><td data-label="Mystic">14</td><td data-label="Technology">12</td><td data-label="Luck">18</td></tr></tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Proficiency</th><th scope="col">Cooking</th><th scope="col">Commerce</th><th scope="col">Communication</th><th scope="col">Rogue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Body Builder</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">3</td><td data-label="Communication">2</td><td data-label="Rogue">2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Scholar</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">6</td><td data-label="Communication">4</td><td data-label="Rogue">2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Salesman</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">15</td><td data-label="Communication">10</td><td data-label="Rogue">3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Computer Expert</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">8</td><td data-label="Communication">3</td><td data-label="Rogue">5</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Musician</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">4</td><td data-label="Communication">7</td><td data-label="Rogue">3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Martial Artist</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">3</td><td data-label="Communication">2</td><td data-label="Rogue">2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Player</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">10</td><td data-label="Communication">9</td><td data-label="Rogue">7</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Games Master</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">8</td><td data-label="Communication">4</td><td data-label="Rogue">4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Athlete</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">5</td><td data-label="Communication">3</td><td data-label="Rogue">2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Magician</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">2</td><td data-label="Communication">3</td><td data-label="Rogue">3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jack of All Trades</th><td data-label="Cooking">1</td><td data-label="Commerce">12</td><td data-label="Communication">5</td><td data-label="Rogue">3</td></tr></tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Proficiency</th><th scope="col">Bedroom action</th><th scope="col">Base reward</th><th scope="col">Base time / drains</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Body Builder</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Lift Weights</td><td data-label="Base reward">Strength +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -30 Energy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Scholar</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Study Research Papers</td><td data-label="Base reward">Intelligence +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Energy, -15 Calm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Salesman</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Practice Sales Pitch</td><td data-label="Base reward">Commerce +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Calm, -15 Energy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Computer Expert</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Work on Code Projects</td><td data-label="Base reward">Wealth=effective Intelligence×2</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Energy, -15 Calm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Musician</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Practice Guitar</td><td data-label="Base reward">Creativity +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Calm, -15 Energy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Martial Artist</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Practice Martial Forms</td><td data-label="Base reward">Ability +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -20 Energy, -10 Calm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Player</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Practice Social Skills</td><td data-label="Base reward">Attractiveness +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -20 Calm, -10 Energy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Games Master</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Plan Game Strategies</td><td data-label="Base reward">Luck +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Energy, -15 Calm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Athlete</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Aerobics Workout</td><td data-label="Base reward">Stamina +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -30 Energy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Magician</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Crystal Meditation</td><td data-label="Base reward">Mystic +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Calm, -15 Energy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jack of All Trades</th><td data-label="Bedroom action">Practice Various Skills</td><td data-label="Base reward">Perception +1</td><td data-label="Base time / drains">45 min; -15 Energy, -15 Calm</td></tr></tbody></table></details><p>Everyone starts with level 1 proficiency equipment, Grimoire and Casual Outfit. Body Builder/Athlete also have level 1 Armor; Scholar/Salesman Formal Outfit; Musician/Player Dating Outfit; Computer Expert a Ranged Weapon; Martial Artist a Melee Weapon. Base supplies include 10 Food and one each of the Health, Energy and Calm recovery supplies.</p><p>For longer days, develop Stamina and recovery. Physical routes benefit from Strength and Ability; magic routes need Mystic plus enough Energy and Calm. Jack of All Trades can enter multiple ordinary careers, while still meeting each job’s attribute and time conditions. The three late combat specialist paths are separate from starting proficiency and can coexist; see <a href="game-systems-specialist-class.html">Specialist Classes</a> for access, benefits and full progression.</p></section>
<section id="en-careers"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Working_Experience_bonuses"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Universal_stat-30_careers"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Proficiency_careers"></span><h2>Careers, skills and Working Experience</h2><p>The corresponding proficiency’s career normally appears at 30 in its relevant effective attribute. A shift has base costs of 60 minutes and 30 Energy, with an 8% chance to raise its work attribute by 1. Location and career hours still apply. Named skills, proficiency equipment, Working Experience and difficulty affect income; inspect the action tooltip for the current result.</p><details><summary>Show ordinary career access and income skills</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Career</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Ordinary proficiency access</th><th scope="col">Attribute / hours</th><th scope="col">Income skill</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Personal Trainer</th><td data-label="Location">City Gym (Uptown)</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Body Builder / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Strength ≥30; 06:00–21:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Berserker Rage ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Teacher</th><td data-label="Location">University Classroom</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Scholar / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Intelligence ≥30; 09:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Material Science ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Car Salesman</th><td data-label="Location">Sports Car Dealer</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Salesman / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Communication ≥30; 09:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Negotiation ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Illusionist</th><td data-label="Location">Mystic Curiosities Shop</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Magician / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Mystic ≥30; 09:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Illusion Weaving ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">IT Specialist</th><td data-label="Location">University Computer Lab</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Computer Expert / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Technology ≥30; 09:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Quantum Computing ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Producer</th><td data-label="Location">Music Studio</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Musician / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Creativity ≥30; 12:00–23:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Song Writing ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sensei</th><td data-label="Location">Dojo</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Martial Artist / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Stamina ≥30; 10:00–22:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Weapon Mastery ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Promoter</th><td data-label="Location">Night Club</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Player / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Charm ≥30; 00:00–03:00 / 21:00–24:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Reputation Management ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gamer</th><td data-label="Location">Retro Arcade</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Games Master / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Luck ≥30; 12:00–22:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Cheating ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Coach</th><td data-label="Location">Basketball Court</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Athlete / Jack of All Trades</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Stamina ≥30; 09:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Leadership ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Chef</th><td data-label="Location">Downtown Restaurant</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Any starting proficiency</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Cooking ≥30; 10:00–22:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Creative Cooking ×2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Broker</th><td data-label="Location">Investment Planning</td><td data-label="Ordinary proficiency access">Any starting proficiency</td><td data-label="Attribute / hours">Commerce ≥30; 09:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Income skill">Market Analysis ×2</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ordinary base pay draws from the effective work attribute through twice that value, then adds 15; its listed skill doubles that component. Broker instead draws between Charm+Communication and Commerce+Intelligence, then adds Luck. Chef also fills Satiation.</p><p>Without the currently active Master upgrade, Jack’s proficiency-career pay component is 70%; Chef and Broker have no such penalty. Active proficiency-equipment level multiplies the corresponding career’s income, including Working Experience money. Ordinary effect uses at most level 5; an acquired and currently active Master upgrade allows level 10. A retained equipment level does not automatically replace the new cycle’s Master upgrade.</p></details><p>Applicable work draws extra pay from 0 through current Working Experience, then advances that experience. Business Acumen doubles the bonus limit; Diligent Worker raises base experience gain from 1 to 2; Responsibility gives a separate 25% chance of+1. Combined levels of the three outfits give another+1 chance at combined level/16, capped at 100%. See <a href="walkthrough-wealth-guide.html">Wealth Guide</a> for the broader income route.</p></section>
<section id="en-learning"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Skill_descriptions_are_not_universal_passives"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="How_skills_are_learned"></span><h2>Choose a learning route</h2><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Method</th><th scope="col">Current rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Starting proficiency</th><td data-label="Current rule">Most ordinary proficiencies grant two starting skills; see <a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a> for the actual pairs.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Crystal Enlightenment</th><td data-label="Current rule">At a Crystal-service location, spend 1 Crystal and zero minutes for a random unknown ordinary skill. Its current 105-skill range does not check the catalogue’s base-stat thresholds.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gonzo’s skill book</th><td data-label="Current rule">At his ordinary-dungeon shop, pay 5 Dragon Coins, or 4 with Negotiation. Preview the random book before confirming. Only unknown ordinary skills meeting its base-stat filter are selected.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Location lessons</th><td data-label="Current rule">Visit the teaching location and meet that action’s own requirements. Learning costs are separate from later skill-use costs.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Character / story routes</th><td data-label="Current rule">Meet the teacher and follow the relevant Objectives. Location, schedule, relationship stage, completed events or access requirements can control the entry. Teacher links open the relevant route guide.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ordinary random learning excludes known skills. Crystals and books have different filters, and other dungeon teaching events use their own conditions. If Gonzo has nothing eligible, inspect Crystal training or a named teacher.</p><p>The purpose column summarizes a skill’s role and confirmed functions. Some skills open activity, job, dialogue or event options without granting a hidden bonus to every related action. Use Combat for complete attack, spell and trigger rules.</p><figure class="reviewed-screenshot" style="max-width: 680px"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: A native Power Strike detail lists its attribute requirement and uses. A detail description alone is not a lesson purchase." href="../assets/images/wiki/skills-guide/en-skill-detail-full.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="A native Power Strike detail lists its attribute requirement and uses. A detail description alone is not a lesson purchase." decoding="async" height="570" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/skills-guide/en-skill-detail.webp" width="640"/></a><figcaption>A native Power Strike detail lists its attribute requirement and uses. A detail description alone is not a lesson purchase.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-choices"><h2>Find a skill for the task</h2><ul><li>Combat Scanner reveals enemy information; use <a href="game-systems-combat-system.html">Combat</a> for attacks, spells and procs.</li><li>Data Mining reveals more numeric information. Gem’s Mining skill is for dwarven dungeon walls. The separate outdoor mining game needs no learned skill; see <a href="game-systems-mining-system.html">Mining</a> for its entry and pickaxes.</li><li>Leadership opens TD’s related attribute; Combat Leadership is a separate skill. Prepare the army with <a href="game-systems-tower-defense.html">Tower Defense</a>.</li><li>Blink provides anchor travel; Shadow Step enables escape from eligible fights. They have different uses.</li><li>The Romantic skill and Romantic relationship stage are separate concepts. Check the character card for a teacher’s stage requirement.</li><li>Known qualifying spells contribute part of Wizard Clout. Keep learning and doing related activities; see <a href="game-systems-wizard-faction.html">Wizard Faction</a>.</li></ul></section>
<section id="en-catalogue-combat"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Skills_and_categories"></span><h2>Combat</h2><details><summary>Show every skill in this group</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Skill</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Current sources</th><th scope="col">Gonzo book base-stat filter</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Acrobatics</th><td data-label="Purpose">Enhanced mobility and evasive maneuvers</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Acrobat Training Hall</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥18</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Adrenaline Rush</th><td data-label="Purpose">Doubles maximum physical attack damage below 30% health</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Stamina ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Archery Focus</th><td data-label="Purpose">Improves TD shot spread, Neural Targeting tracking, and Darts/Archery perfect-power zones.</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-riki.html">Riki</a>; <a href="character-robin.html">Robin</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Perception ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Battle Meditation</th><td data-label="Purpose">Combat recovery involving Energy and Health.</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Monk's Temple Training Hall</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Mystic ≥10</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Berserker Rage</th><td data-label="Purpose">Massive damage boost with health cost</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-yrsa.html">Yrsa</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Strength ≥20</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Combat Leadership</th><td data-label="Purpose">Boost ally effectiveness</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Fighters Guild</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Charm ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Combat Reflexes</th><td data-label="Purpose">Resist web effects</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-anthrax.html">Anthrax</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Counterattack</th><td data-label="Purpose">Counterattack-themed choices in encounters and conversations</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-lilu.html">Master Lilu</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥18</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Defensive Stance</th><td data-label="Purpose">Passively reduces physical damage by up to 10%</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-valkyra.html">Valkyra</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Stamina ≥12</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Disarming Technique</th><td data-label="Purpose">Quick Attack and Sovereign Edge have a 10% disarm chance per action; the enemy's next damaging action deals half damage</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-lilu.html">Master Lilu</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥20</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Endurance Training</th><td data-label="Purpose">Reduces negative Energy adjustments; useful for repeated activities.</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Knight's Training Grounds</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Stamina ≥30</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Exploit Weakness</th><td data-label="Purpose">Find and target enemy vulnerabilities</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-lilu.html">Master Lilu</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Intelligence ≥16</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fleet Footed</th><td data-label="Purpose">Improved chance to flee from combat</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-lilu.html">Master Lilu</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Intimidating Presence</th><td data-label="Purpose">Frighten enemies</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-yrsa.html">Yrsa</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Strength ≥18</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Iron Constitution</th><td data-label="Purpose">Reduces some Health costs and supports physical resilience.</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Human Performance Optimization Lab</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Strength ≥30</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Iron Will</th><td data-label="Purpose">Resist sleep, charm, and disorientation</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Underground Modification Clinic</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Stamina ≥16</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Martial Arts</th><td data-label="Purpose">Unarmed combat mastery</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pain Tolerance</th><td data-label="Purpose">Increases your effective armor level by 1</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Bio-Optimization Medical Center</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Stamina ≥18</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Power Strike</th><td data-label="Purpose">Enhanced melee damage</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-valkyra.html">Valkyra</a>; Fighters Guild</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Strength ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Quick Draw</th><td data-label="Purpose">Faster weapon deployment</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; Entertainment Tower</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥20</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Shadow Step</th><td data-label="Purpose">Guaranteed escape from eligible fights; boss restrictions still apply.</td><td data-label="Current sources"><a href="character-shadow.html">Shadow</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">— (specific source)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Side-Step</th><td data-label="Purpose">Upgrades Quick Attack with a 20% chance to dodge the enemy's next attack and strike again</td><td data-label="Current sources"><a href="character-valkyra.html">Valkyra</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">— (specific source)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Skull Crusher</th><td data-label="Purpose">Upgrades Power Strike with +10% base damage and a 30% chance for devastating 4 x damage</td><td data-label="Current sources"><a href="character-yrsa.html">Yrsa</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">— (specific source)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sovereign Edge</th><td data-label="Purpose">Upgrades basic Attack with Coradio's perfected sword discipline, including rare decapitation and mortal blow strikes</td><td data-label="Current sources"><a href="character-coradio.html">Coradio</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">— (specific source)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Stormslash</th><td data-label="Purpose">A physical attack using Strength and Ability; see Combat.</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-muramasa.html">Muramasa</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥22</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Swordplay</th><td data-label="Purpose">Reduced miss chance for physical attacks</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-valkyra.html">Valkyra</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥20</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tactical Awareness</th><td data-label="Purpose">Predict enemy moves</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-artemis.html">Artemis</a>; <a href="character-neena.html">Neena</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Intelligence ≥15</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tai-Chi</th><td data-label="Purpose">A 5% chance to reflect 5% of incoming damage back to the attacker. Bonuses scale with True Neutral alignment</td><td data-label="Current sources"><a href="character-lilu.html">Master Lilu</a></td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">— (specific source)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Weapon Mastery</th><td data-label="Purpose">Proficiency with all weapon types</td><td data-label="Current sources">Ordinary random learning; <a href="character-anthrax.html">Anthrax</a>; <a href="character-valkyra.html">Valkyra</a>; Fighters Guild</td><td data-label="Gonzo book base-stat filter">Ability ≥18</td></tr></tbody></table></details></section>
